00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:02.860
Hey guys it's Jan here.

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:07.970
As the second instalment in the DC Extended
Universe, Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:13.099
firmly establishes Superman, Batman, and Wonder
Woman and sets up numerous future movies like

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:15.410
Suicide Squad and Justice League.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:19.750
The film is stacked with homages and hidden
references to the many Batman and Superman

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:24.429
films before it as well as the comic books,
so I've put together all the easter eggs and

00:00:24.429 --> 00:00:26.919
references I could find in this video.

00:00:26.919 --> 00:00:30.050
Of course, I'd love to hear about any others
you've spotted too.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:34.550
Just before that, I've got an awesome giveaway
thanks to our friends at Titan Books, so if

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:39.280
you'd like the chance to win this fantastic
hardback book Batman v Superman: Dawn of Justice:

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.870
The Art of the Film which is packed with stunning
concept art, storyboards, blueprints, costume

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:49.399
detail and behind-the-scenes shots from the
set, then make sure you subscribe and leave

00:00:49.399 --> 00:00:52.450
a comment about your favourite easter egg
from the movie.

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:56.899
For more details and ways to enter, check
out the Gleam link in the video description

00:00:56.899 --> 00:00:57.899
below!

00:00:57.899 --> 00:01:01.039
And a quick warning, there will be spoilers
ahead so if you haven't seen the movie yet,

00:01:01.039 --> 00:01:03.450
check out my non-spoiler review here!

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:07.780
The Dark Knight Returns by Frank Miller was
a major influence on Batman v Superman, and

00:01:07.780 --> 00:01:11.460
when Batman jumps on the side of a building
during the showdown with Doomsday it's a visual

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.390
homage to the cover of the comic book series.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:18.030
Doomsday's look, his bony protrusions and
claw-like arm are similar to his look in The

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.250
Death of Superman by Dan Jurgens.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:24.530
And Superman's final moments with Lois Lane,
his pivotal battle and death at the hands

00:01:24.530 --> 00:01:28.150
of the supervillain are also references to
this seminal comic book.

00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:32.840
The coffin for Superman's state burial recalls
a similar one used when Superman died battling

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:38.250
Doomsday in the animated movie Superman Doomsday
in which Superman comes back from the dead.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:42.690
And during the final scene at the Kent family
burial ground, you can hear a few light thumps

00:01:42.690 --> 00:01:46.770
in the music that resemble a heartbeat, a
hint that Superman will be coming back to

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:51.890
life, and likely a nod to the way Batman faked
his death in The Dark Knight Returns by slowing

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:53.080
his heartbeat.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:57.340
And the earth which starts to move and float
up in the very final shot recalls the way

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:02.170
the earth moved around Superman's fists when
he first learned how to fly in Man of Steel.

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:05.820
The movie introduces Wonder Woman and she
sports a number of her classic tools and weapons

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:10.450
from the comics including her Wonder Woman
tiara, belt, bulletproof bracelets and Lasso

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:11.450
of Truth.

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:15.330
And her shield might also be a nod to the
Amazonian Magic Sphere from the comics which

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:16.580
had mystical properties.

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:20.920
As Diana Prince, she also wears a range of
gold jewellery which are nods to her Wonder

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:22.300
Woman logo and accessories.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:26.470
And at Lex Luthor's party when Bruce Wayne
chases after Diana Prince who's stolen his

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:30.830
hacking device, he has to avoid a cake or
a model of a Greek temple being taken out

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:35.020
to the party, which a visual reference to
Wonder Woman's Amazonian background from Greek

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.360
mythology.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.410
Lex Luthor starts the film with a full head
of hair but, when his head is shaven in prison,

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:43.650
he ends up with his more common bald look
from the comics.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:47.030
And if you look carefully at the prison guards
on either side of him, you'll see they have

00:02:47.030 --> 00:02:50.860
Belle Reve badges on their uniforms, which
means he's likely going to come into contact

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:52.230
with the Suicide Squad!

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:58.370
And Lex Luthor's prisoner number 16-TK-421
is an easter egg to the Stormtrooper TK-421

00:02:58.370 --> 00:03:02.590
who was ambushed by Han Solo in Star Wars:
A New Hope.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:06.440
Martha Kent works as a waitress at Ralli's
Diner, a nod to the Superman comics where

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:10.530
Lex Luthor visits the Ralli's Diner and makes
a fake proposal to a waitress to give her

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:13.700
a million dollars if she spends a month with
him in Metropolis.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:17.630
The Mark of Zorro movie poster in the flashback
to the murder of Bruce Wayne's parents is

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:20.360
an homage to the same moment in the comics.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:23.810
The movie Excalibur also gets a reference
which could be a nod to the time-travelling

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:28.410
story in the comics where Batman and Superman
travel back together to King Arthur's Camelot.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:32.821
Later in Bruce's dream of blood seeping out
of his parents' tombs, he has a vision of

00:03:32.821 --> 00:03:37.130
a creature which looks a lot like Man-Bat,
Batman's enemy from the comics.

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:41.260
And Alfred's line the next day about an empty
wine cellar and the next generation of Waynes

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:44.090
is a line of dialogue taken straight from
The Dark Knight Returns.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:49.020
Oh, and the look of Batman's heavily armoured
suit which he puts on to face off with Superman

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:54.080
is reminiscent of the same suit Batman used
to battle Superman in The Dark Knight Returns.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:58.400
When Bruce Wayne asks Clark Kent whether he
owns the Daily Planet, it's a nod to the comics

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:01.240
in which Bruce Wayne became the owner of the
Daily Planet.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:06.250
Perry White's line that "this isn't 1938"
is a reference to the year when Superman debuted

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:08.290
on the cover of Action Comics.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:13.430
The 300 on the Russian rocket is a nod to
Frank Miller's 300 comic book series and the

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.720
movie adaptation directed by Zack Snyder.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:20.320
Superman getting nuked and then being revived
by the power of the sun is a callback to a

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:24.340
similar moment when Superman is struck by
a missile in The Dark Knight Returns.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:28.950
And when Superman is shot with Batman's kryptonite,
it's another reference to Frank Miller's comic

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:33.350
in which Oliver Queen shoots Superman with
synthetic kryptonite that Bruce Wayne has

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:34.350
developed.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:37.900
Lana Lang, Clark Kent's romantic interest
in the comics when he was growing up, gets

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:42.290
a nod in Kevin Costner's cameo as Clark's
father and his story about accidentally flooding

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:43.290
the Lang's Farm.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:48.700
And of course, as the title suggests, Batman
v Superman: Dawn of Justice sets up the DC

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.990
Extended Universe for the Justice League movies.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:55.690
And we get some big hints at the likely big
villain of the Justice League, Darkseid.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:05:00.150
In Batman's Knightmare, he looks out over
a desolate landscape where you can see Darkseid's

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.850
Omega symbol in the ground.

00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:06.920
And the insect-like creatures which attack
him later are most likely Darkseid's parademons.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:10.710
The soldiers dressed in black uniforms, who
are working with the parademons and kneel

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:15.040
before Superman, suggest that we might get
a corrupted Superman in the future if he's

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:19.710
resurrected and also might hint that Superman
will be controlled by Darkseid.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:24.300
The hints at Lois' death and a tyrannical
Superman with his own soldiers also reference

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:27.850
the storyline in the videogame Injustice:
Gods Among Us.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:31.550
The way Flash appeared to Batman at the end
of his nightmare with the message "Lois is

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:35.750
the key" recalls the Flashpoint comics where
Barry Allen travels to Batman with a letter

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:37.600
from his father Thomas Wayne.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:41.310
And The Flash also appeared later again in
the meta-human file that Bruce Wayne decrypted

00:05:41.310 --> 00:05:45.350
which, by the way, is titled 'Red Streak',
which is an easter egg to one of the aliases

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:47.860
for Grant Gustin's Flash on the CW's show.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:52.790
There was also a tease to Wonder Woman's solo
movie with a photo of her in Belgium in 1918

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:56.830
at the end of World War I, alongside Chris
Pine's character Steve Trevor.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:06:01.080
There's also an interesting look at the creation
of Cyborg, who gets his own solo movie in

00:06:01.080 --> 00:06:02.080
2020.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:06.370
His father Silas Stone is working to help
his wounded son Vic at STAR Labs when a box

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:07.450
is activated.

00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:12.290
The box hovers over to Vic's body and starts
growing him new cybernetic arms and legs.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:16.389
The scene is a nod to Cyborg's origin story
in the Justice League comics where he's injured

00:06:16.389 --> 00:06:20.450
by an exploding mother box before he's repaired
by his father to become Cyborg.

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:25.090
By the way, when Lex Luthor says "ding ding
ding" in his cell it's a reference to the

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:28.090
ping sound the mother boxes often make in
the comics.

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:32.530
According to his video footage, Aquaman appears
to be located in the Tonga Trench and we not

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:37.250
only get to see his trident, but also see
him do his comic-book-style superspeed swimming

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.139
as he zooms off at the end of his cameo.

00:06:39.139 --> 00:06:43.540
And there's another Aquaman nod in a Daily
Planet newspaper story about water testing

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:47.960
being put on hold due to funding cuts, which
hints at possible pollution that could affect

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:48.960
Aquaman.

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:53.160
There's a Game of Thrones Dothraki easter
egg to Jason Momoa's Khal Drogo in the words

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:56.820
"blood of my blood" which Lex Luthor says
during the creation of Doomsday.

00:06:56.820 --> 00:07:01.110
And there's a King Kong-style moment when
Doomsday leaps to the top of the Lexcorp tower

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:06.260
and is then attacked from the air by helicopters,
and gives a King Kong-like roar of fury.

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:10.530
By the way, as Bruce Wayne starts decrypting
the file he's recovered from Lexcorp, the

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:14.810
name Leech appears on the computer screen,
a little nod to Rex Leech who appeared for

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:18.240
the first time in the comics during the funeral
procession for Superman.

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:22.340
When Diana Prince looks at the files on the
metahumans who Luthor been investigating,

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:27.110
you can see their logos are versions of the
official logos released for each of the solo

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:29.340
movies for the new members of the Justice
League.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:33.350
And Lex Luthor's words about Zeus, Prometheus,
and a thunderbolt is a tease for the superhero

00:07:33.350 --> 00:07:37.170
Shazam who has the power of Living Lightning
in the comic books and who will be getting

00:07:37.170 --> 00:07:39.020
a solo movie in 2019.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:43.240
There's also a stack of easter eggs for classic
Batman villain The Joker who will be appearing

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:44.450
in Suicide Squad.

00:07:44.450 --> 00:07:48.669
Jack Nicholson who played the Joker in Tim
Burton's Batman movie gets a name-check in

00:07:48.669 --> 00:07:51.440
the sign for Nicholson Terminal &amp; Dock Company.

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:55.350
Bruce Wayne's line about having a bad history
with "freaks dressed like clowns" is also

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:59.900
an amusing nod to the Joker, and the defaced
Robin costume hints at the Batman comic A

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:04.370
Death In The Family in which the Joker brutally
beat Jason Todd with a crowbar and then killed

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:05.370
him.

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:08.700
There's a bunch more Joker easter eggs hidden
in the graffiti in the dilapidated building

00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:13.639
where Batman and Superman face off, with plays
on the Joker's name such as "Joe + Kayla",

00:08:13.639 --> 00:08:18.220
the word Jokey repeated three times on a column
and another "Joe" with an arrow that points

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.680
to letters K and R on another column.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:25.160
And Batman villain The Riddler gets an easter
egg via a question mark graffiti on a column.

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:29.910
Other graffiti include Aphrodite, the Greek
goddess who appears in the Wonder Woman comics,

00:08:29.910 --> 00:08:32.909
and Enos which is a reference to Clay Enos,
who's the stills photographer on Man of Steel,

00:08:32.909 --> 00:08:35.180
Batman v Superman, and Wonder Woman.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:39.000
When Bruce Wayne clones the cell-phone of
Anatoly, the Russian criminal working for

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:43.450
Lex Luthor, it's a callback to Nolan's Dark
Knight movie when Lucius Fox uses a cell phone

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:46.850
to scan and record a map of Chinese mob boss
Lau's building.

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:51.270
By the way, Anatoly's character is based on
KGBeast from the comics and in the Blackest

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:55.310
Night Batman comic series he's resurrected
and becomes one of the Black Lantern Corps,

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:59.430
so even though Batman probably killed him
in this movie, it's possible we could see

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:01.260
him come back in a future film.

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:04.750
And when Bruce Wayne says to Anatoly that
he knows a bit of Russian as he spent three

00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:08.910
nights with a Bolshoi ballerina, it's a callback
to The Dark Knight movie when Bruce Wayne

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:13.339
dated a Russian prima ballerina and went on
a cruise ship with the Russian ballet as cover

00:09:13.339 --> 00:09:15.029
for his investigation on Lau.

00:09:15.029 --> 00:09:19.620
Jeremy Iron's Alfred makes fun of the various
incarnations of Batman's raspy voice when

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:22.330
he's playing around with Batman's voice modulator.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:26.790
And Alfred's line that the White Portuguese
might be a phantasm is a little verbal shout-out

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:29.650
to the animated Batman film, Mask of the Phantasm.

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:33.820
By the way, the name "Penobscot" on this building
in Metropolis is a reference to the Penobscot

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:39.330
County Probate Court where Christopher Richardson
petitioned in 2016 to legally change his first

00:09:39.330 --> 00:09:40.570
name to Batman.

00:09:40.570 --> 00:09:45.760
Superman nearly drowning in water with kryptonite
and being rescued by Lois Lane recalls when

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:49.410
he almost drowned because of a kryptonite
necklace that Lex Luthor put on him in the

00:09:49.410 --> 00:09:54.870
1978 Superman movie and in that movie Superman
was saved by Lex Luthor's girlfriend.

00:09:54.870 --> 00:09:58.460
Bruce Wayne's disparaging remark about the
Daily Planet publishing articles about Superman

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:03.700
saving cats is a nod to the times in the comics
and the 1978 movie that Superman rescues a

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:04.700
cat.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:08.839
Clark Kent's dog Shelby from Smallville gets
a mention in a street sign for "Shelby Street"

00:10:08.839 --> 00:10:09.920
in Metropolis.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:14.630
The Smallville talk show "Good Morning, Metropolis"
also gets a shoutout with a twist when Perry

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:17.420
White says "Good morning, Smallville" to Clark
Kent.

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:21.170
And during the discussion between Perry White
and Clark Kent about what the newspaper should

00:10:21.170 --> 00:10:25.790
be reporting, Perry says to Clark "The American
conscience died with Robert, Martin and John"

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:29.480
a reference to the line in Frank Miller's
The Dark Knight Returns that "The American

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:31.170
conscience died with the Kennedys."

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:36.080
And it's also a reference to the 1968 song
Abraham, Martin and John, which is a tribute

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:40.350
to the assassinated John and Robert Kennedy,
Martin Luther King, and Abraham Lincoln.

00:10:40.350 --> 00:10:44.940
Perry White also references The Wizard of
Oz when he asks where Clark Kent is, and jokes

00:10:44.940 --> 00:10:47.990
that he "clicks his heels three times and
goes back to Kansas."

00:10:47.990 --> 00:10:52.130
And the Emerald City is also mentioned by
Lex Luthor when he's talking about the kryptonite

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.170
in the Indian Ocean.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:59.240
Carla Gugino returns from Man of Steel where
she voiced the Kryptonian robot Kelor.

00:10:59.240 --> 00:11:04.690
Gugino worked with Zack Snyder previously
playing Madam Gorski in his movie Sucker Punch.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:08.480
And at the Daily Planet offices, there's a
name plaque for Picture Editor Liz Ritenour,

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:11.580
who was an art department assistant on the
movie.

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:15.980
Speaking of crew name-checks, stunt coordinator
Tim Rigby also gets a nod with the name Rigby

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:19.820
appearing on one of the mail boxes belonging
to Lois Lane's neighbours.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:22.470
And there's a cameo at the very beginning
of the movie by Jimmy Olsen.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:26.590
He isn't named but he's the CIA op posing
as a photographer who gets shot.

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:31.180
He's played by actor Michael Cassidy who previously
played Grant Gabriel, a clone of Lex Luthor's

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:32.350
brother in Smallville.

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:36.220
By the way, Zack Synder has said that he originally
wanted to cast Jesse Eisenberg as Jimmy Olsen,

00:11:36.220 --> 00:11:39.770
with the role of Lex Luthor possibly going
to Bryan Cranston.

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:44.290
So guys, what other easter eggs and references
did you spot in Batman v Superman?

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:45.630
And which was your favourite?

